            "r": "C5"
          },
          {
            "v": "Raw capture exports use their supplied message-type representation; derived/session sources may encode the same protocol concept numerically. Preserve the source representation and consult the source tab.",
            "s": "10",
            "r": "D5"
          },
          {
            "v": "Example: `Announce` is a PTP message name; numeric forms are encoded representations.",
            "s": "10",
            "r": "E5"
          },
          {
            "v": "A change can describe packet role/order, not receiver selection or maliciousness.",
            "s": "10",
            "r": "F5"
          },
          {
            "v": "S026/S027 raw-capture tabs and source-specific derived tabs",
            "s": "10",
            "r": "G5"
          }
        ]
